  9	/**
 10	 * What evaluating one piece of example code produced.
 11	 *
 12	 * Example code is arbitrary program text, so it either produces a value or
 13	 * raises something. Both come back as this value rather than as a return and a
 14	 * thrown exception, which keeps the one place that runs untrusted text — and so
 15	 * the one broad catch doctest needs — inside ExpressionEvaluator.
